  "formula": {
    "buy_v2": "q=floor(amount*vqr/(vtr-amount))+1",
    "buy_exact_quote_in_v2_whitelist": "q=input; amount=floor(vtr*(q-1)/(vqr+q-1)); input covers zero protocol/creator fees",
    "sell_v2": "q=floor(amount*vqr/(vtr+amount))",
    "post_curve": "Buy subtracts amount from both token reserves and adds q to both quote reserves; sell reverses those signs.",
    "sync": "D=2*token_total_supply-post_base_vault-post_base_user; vqr=floor((D+post_vtr)*post_rqr/D), then native/token cap; all proposed values remain below cap."
  },
  "execution_requirements": [
    "Do not change owner, executable flag, base token balances or token mint supply. All base token accounts retain captured typed owners and authorities.",
    "Change only documented curve reserve/flag fields, its ordinary lamports for native backing, and Global.whitelist_pda for the enabled test.",
    "Use the existing signed local user and loaded captured dependencies; no RPC or live-chain submission.",
    "For token cases create normal initialized SPL mint/token accounts with the existing fixture builder, keeping mint, authority and PDA validation active.",
    "Record complete transaction bytes, signatures, Clock and non-target account prestates for each side before execution.",
    "Require original success and exact original/candidate error, state, CPI, event, return data and ordered log agreement.",
    "Independently derive actual post-CPI base balances and sync formula; positive cases must differ from the no-sync reserve.",
    "Deduplicate executed inputs against all prior corpus inputs using transaction bytes plus full non-target-account prestate and Clock; do not claim new cases from the eight definitions alone.",
    "Use the main contract buy_v2, buy_exact_quote_in_v2 and sell_v2 account layouts and original captured dependency programs. Keep the supplied Token-2022 base mint and both original base accounts unchanged before the trade.",
    "Set Global.whitelist_pda to the existing normally signed fixture user in every proposed case. Use existing validated reserved fee recipient for mode-enabled inputs and the existing ordinary recipient for the mode-disabled controls.",
    "For token-quote cases use the existing V2 builder to create a normal initialized USDC-like SPL mint and canonical quote token accounts; use no transfer-fee or hook extensions for these focused cases.",
    "Native buy_v2 instruction_limit is a maximum total quote cost; exact buy and sell limits are minimum output. Keep partial-fill false.",
    "Check post-CPI base balances, curve reserves and both event quote-reserve fields against the explicit numbers above; mode-disabled controls must equal the no-sync reserve.",
    "Do not treat these 12 definitions as novel executed cases until prestate/transaction/Clock deduplication against retained corpora is complete."
  ],
  "optional_future_guard_control": "If root wants direct false-whitelist coverage in each V2 wrapper, clone one native positive per operation with the retained original whitelist. Retain normal configured fees and derive its quote/amount using the existing fee CPI result. Do not assume fee-zero exact-buy math for that control; those three inputs are not included in this twelve-case proposal.",
